quizQuestions.question:
Consider the following code:
```javascript
let a = 10;
let b = "10";
console.log(a === b);
```
What output is displayed in the Console?

Consider the following code:
```javascript
const buah = ["Apel", "Jeruk", "Mangga"];
console.log(buah[1]);
```
What output is produced?

Consider the following code:
```javascript
const kuadrat = (x) => x * x;
console.log(kuadrat(6));
```
What output value is printed?

Consider the following code:
```javascript
const angka = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const hasil = angka.filter((n) => n > 3);
console.log(hasil.length);
```
What output is produced?

Consider the following code:
```javascript
let hitung = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  hitung += 2;
}
console.log(hitung);
```
What output is displayed in the Console?

Consider the following code:
```javascript
const nama = "Budi";
const salam = `Halo ${nama}!`;
console.log(salam);
```
What text is printed in the Console?

courses.cheatSheetMarkdown:
# JavaScript Fundamentals Cheat Sheet

## Variables & Data Types
- `const nama = "Budi";` (constant value, top priority)
- `let skor = 0;` (mutable value)
- Strict comparison: `===` and `!==`

## Functions & Arrays
```javascript
const tambah = (a, b) => a + b;
const angka = [1, 2, 3, 4];
const genap = angka.filter((n) => n % 2 === 0);
```

## DOM Manipulation & Events
```javascript
const btn = document.querySelector("#btn");
const teks = document.querySelector("#hasil");

btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
  teks.textContent = "Tombol diklik!";
});
```

